      "message": "(Continued from PS4)\n\n1. Run-time parameters instead of compile-time parameters is fine. (i.e., template is not necessary.)\n2. I appreciate the fact that we\u0027ll need more parameters later. But...\n   a) It\u0027s better to add complexity as needed, rather than all up-front. This is for two reasons. First: reviewers don\u0027t know what\u0027s coming later, so they don\u0027t know why the additional complexity is necessary. Second: adding complexity as-needed avoids adding accumulating cruft that turned out not to be necessary. [i]\n   b) Given the number of call-sites that only need a single packet, I still think it\u0027s worth making the single-packet case simpler.\n\n  We could, for example, have AppendMessageAndReturn, for the single-packet case, and AppendMultipleMessagesAndReturn, for the multi-packet case.\n\n[i] There are exceptions to this, of course. If the needs down-the-line are so different from the immediate need that a large refactor would be necessary, then it makes sense to discuss with reviewers about the CLs that are coming down the line.\n\n(FWIW: if the number of response packets is known at compile time, we could use a variadic template to cover all cases. But I mention that more as trivia, than as a recommendation.)",
